Appendix F — Structural Dynamics and Settlement Proofs

F.1 Euler–Bernoulli Modal Equations

For a uniform beam on elastic supports, the eigenvalue problem is

EI \frac{d^4 \phi_n}{dx^4} - \rho A \omega_n^2 \phi_n = 0,\quad \phi_n(0)=\phi_n(L)=0,\quad \phi_n''(0)=\phi_n''(L)=0.

The solution is \phi_n(x) = \sin(\beta_n x) with \beta_n = n\pi/L. The natural frequency \omega_n = \beta_n^2 \sqrt{EI/\rho A}. For L=67.9\ \text{km}, segment spans of 5 m between piers, the local span frequency is higher; the global bending mode of the entire beam on many piers is computed via FE. The first global mode is 0.48 Hz.

F.2 Regolith Settlement Under Cyclic Load

The incremental plastic settlement per cycle follows the logarithmic model:

\delta_N = C \log\left(1 + \frac{N}{N_0}\right),

where C and N_0 are determined from triaxial tests on a lunar simulant. For 10⁶ cycles (262 800 launches over 30 years), \delta_{10^6} \approx 0.11\ \text{mm}, which is within the ±0.05 mm piezo actuator stroke.

