Appendix I — Economic Model Derivation

The levelised cost of payload delivery is

\text{LCO} = \frac{ \text{CRF} \cdot \text{CapEx} + \text{OpEx} }{ \dot{m} },

with \text{CRF} = \frac{r(1+r)^N}{(1+r)^N-1}. Using r=0.05, N=30\ \text{yr}, CRF = 0.06505, CapEx = 92\times 10^9, OpEx = 0.08\times 10^9 $/yr, and \dot{m}=1.752\times 10^6\ \text{kg/yr},

\text{LCO} = \frac{ 0.06505\times 92\times 10^9 + 0.08\times 10^9 }{ 1.752\times 10^6 } = \frac{5.98\times10^9 + 0.08\times10^9}{1.752\times10^6} \approx 3460\ \text{\$/kg}.

Sensitivity: reducing the discount rate to 3% (CRF=0.0512) and increasing lifetime to 40 yr (CRF=0.0433) drops the annual capital charge; with a learning‑curve cost reduction of 20% on CapEx, the mature LCO reaches ~2100 $/kg. Further reductions require higher throughput or lower launch costs.

